+---
+id: task-002-record-task-creation-and-change-times
+type: task
+title: "Record task creation and change times"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Record task creation and change times
+
+Record when each task was created and when it was last changed, so the app can show how old a task is
+and what changed recently.
+
+## What it asks
+
+- Every `Task` has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, both ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- When a task is added, `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are the same.
+- Every change to a task sets its `updatedAt` to the time of the change: completing, reopening,
+  renaming, tagging and untagging it. `createdAt` never changes.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **The clock comes from outside the domain.** The domain may not read the clock
+  (`r3-no-clock-or-randomness`), so `createTodoList` takes an optional clock, `now: () => string`, and
+  the domain functions receive the time as a plain string. The default clock, used by the app, is
+  `new Date().toISOString()`; it lives in `src/index.ts`, which is outside `src/domain/`.
+- **Every successful change bumps `updatedAt`.** A call that succeeds is a change, including a rename to
+  the task's own title and a tag or untag call. A failed call changes nothing and keeps `updatedAt`.
+- **Timestamps are tested with a fixed clock**, so the tests stay deterministic.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `add` returns a task whose `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are equal ISO-8601 strings.
+- Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging and untagging a task each set `updatedAt` to the clock's time
+  and leave `createdAt` as it was.
+- A failed change (for example completing a task twice, or a duplicate rename) leaves the task's
+  `updatedAt` unchanged.
+- `get`, `find` and `list` return the timestamps as stored.
